\\
801.41;+42216,;35~WP-start~21
NEWS Score: 0-2 (Low)\\
     Continue to monitor per facility policy\\
\\NEWS Score: 3-4 (Medium)\\
     Assess threat, confer with site-specific nursing resource, assess\\
      if acute illness or unstable chronic disease.\\
     Score of 3 in any one parameter, reassess VS and parameter in\\ 
      1 hour.\\
     Score increases from more than one parameter, increase frequency\\
      of VS to 2 hours, repeat NEWS\\
\\NEWS Score: 5-6 (High)\\
     Your patient is at risk to deteriorate rapidly.\\
     Contact provider and site-specific nursing resources.\\
     Increase VS every 2 hours x 3 (6 hours total); reassess NEWS with\\
      each VS set\\
     Score of 3 in any one parameter, reassess VS and parameter in\\
      1 hour.\\
\\NEWS Score: = or > 7 (Immediate Action)\\
     Call RRT, notify charge RN and primary team immediately.\\
     Notify site-specific nursing resource and activate Rapid Response\\
      immediately.\\
     Continuous monitoring of VS is recommended.
